{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"immobile-drastic-springtail","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\nResearch how agents can write concise but complete ticket descriptions, plans, and comments. Use current 2026 evidence and examples from popular, actively maintained OSS prompt, skill, or Claude-plugin projects.\n\n## Plan\n- Review recent primary research on controllable verbosity, compression, and evaluation.\n- Inspect maintained OSS agent-instruction repositories for concrete brevity patterns.\n- Synthesize authoring guidance and deterministic bloat signals, including false-positive safeguards.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The answer cites dated sources and separates research evidence from practitioner convention.\n- It gives actionable guidance for agents without sacrificing necessary facts.\n- It proposes deterministic, implementable checks with thresholds, severity, and exemptions.\n- It identifies checks that should remain advisory because they cannot prove irrelevance.","id":"ee0c-1d25-1652-43c3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["research","agents","writing-quality"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Research concise agent-authored ticket content"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788399027082733146,"uuid":"0f883e31-48db-4539-8413-0545048465e0"}